  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This report summarizes federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Total federal contract obligations equal $18.6B. The Department of Energy leads agency spending with $6.1B in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $5.6B in obligations. The Department of Homeland Security and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration each have $1.2B in obligations. The General Services Administration obligated $866M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $855M, and the Department of Justice obligated $775M. The Department of the Treasury obligated $547M, the Department of Transportation obligated $318M, and the Department of Agriculture obligated $316M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial because totals reflect fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies lead federal contract obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $6.1B, making it the largest agency by contract obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $5.6B, the next largest agency. The Department of Homeland Security and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration each obligated $1.2B. Several civilian agencies, including the General Services Administration and the Department of Health and Human Services, also show sizable obligations at $866M and $855M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How do smaller agencies compare in contract obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $775M, while the Department of the Treasury obligated $547M. The Department of Transportation obligated $318M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $316M. These figures are part of total federal contract obligations of $18.6B for FY2027 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
